# A write beneath a disjunction of structs in the target.
-- source.cue --
a: string
-- target.cue --
rootfield: {branch: 1, one: string} | {branch: 2, two: string}
-- lens.cue --
input: _
result: {rootfield: {branch: 1, one: input.a}}
-- out --
unknown
result.rootfield.branch is written beneath result.rootfield, which is a disjunction in the target schema; the checker descends only into a single struct or list, so write result.rootfield as one value (rule unknown-target-constraint) @ lens.cue:2:22
result.rootfield.one is written beneath result.rootfield, which is a disjunction in the target schema; the checker descends only into a single struct or list, so write result.rootfield as one value (rule unknown-target-constraint) @ lens.cue:2:38
